WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.540
KARIM LAKHANI: Crowdsourcing is a
subset within open innovation, where

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:09.940
we rely on hundreds if not thousands of
people working in parallel sometimes,

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.460
competitively or collaboratively, to go
solve problems that we may care about.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:20.050
Crowdsourcing basically burst
into the scene in the early 2000s

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:24.100
when we started to see
companies and platforms emerge

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:29.140
that relied on the wisdom of the crowd
to help us write Wikipedia articles.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.010
To help us write software code.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:33.970
And to even solve the
toughest science problems.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.860
So crowdsourcing fits in within
this broader paradigm that ideas

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.990
reside outside of the company.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:43.660
And the best ways for
a company to innovate

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:47.850
is to often go to the outside
world and bring it in.

